Five TZif files of the IANA time zone database, release 2026d, as the
system's /usr/share/zoneinfo had them: Europe/Madrid, America/New_York,
Asia/Kolkata, Australia/Sydney and Pacific/Chatham, the file name the
zone's with _ for /. The tests of the local clock (pastime's zone,
SysUtils' local time, P131) run with TZ set to these files, so their
output is the same on every machine whatever its own tzdata; the
expected outputs were written by Go's time package with the same TZ.

The files are in the public domain, as the tz database's LICENSE says:
"Unless specified below, all files in the tz code and data (including
this LICENSE file) are in the public domain."
